@* ColorSchemeSwitch's Overview, written by hand after IzzyTheme's: the three looks (previewed in
   each mode), where the choice is kept, following it from C# (Interactive) and its own words. The Light
   and dark article has the rest. Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A color scheme switch is a control for choosing System, Light or Dark for the whole app. It suits any app with a dark scheme. Put it in the header, once. The <Anchor Href="docs/components/izzy-theme">IzzyTheme</Anchor> in the <Code>head</Code> sets the scheme every page arrives in. <Anchor Href="docs/theming/color-scheme">Light and dark</Anchor> covers the default scheme and a scheme for part of a page.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Menu, toggle and segmented</Heading>
<TextBlock>The switch comes in three looks. Set <Code>Variant</Code> to choose one:</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Look</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Menu</Code> (default)</td><td>An icon button that opens System, Light and Dark.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Toggle</Code></td><td>One button that switches between light and dark.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Segmented</Code></td><td>The three side by side. To show icons alone, set <Code>IconOnly</Code>.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>
<ExampleViewer Example="color-scheme-switch-variants" />
<TextBlock>These switches share the user's choice with this site's own switch, so picking one here changes this site's scheme too. <Code>Toggle</Code> has no way back to System, so use it where following the device isn't needed.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Where the choice is kept</Heading>
<TextBlock>The choice is saved in the <Code>ib-scheme</Code> cookie. IzzyTheme reads it on the server, so every later page arrives in that scheme with no flash. <Code>AddIzzyBlazor()</Code> lets the server read it.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="csharp" Title="Program.cs">@Setup</Code>
<TextBlock><Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">With JavaScript off</Anchor>, the switch is hidden, and pages follow the device or a choice saved earlier.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Binding the color scheme</Heading>
<TextBlock>On interactive pages, you can read the user's choice and set a scheme from C#. To learn the choice, handle <Code>ValueChanged</Code>. To apply a scheme to the page, the cookie and other open tabs, set <Code>Value</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="color-scheme-switch-bound" />
<TextBlock>To show the choice saved in the cookie, leave <Code>Value</Code> unset. A bound value that starts null does the same until the user picks something.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The switch has a name for screen readers, and its options and toggle have words of their own.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Label</Code></td><td>The menu button's or group's name</td><td>"Color scheme"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>
<TextBlock>The options' words ("System", "Light", "Dark") and the toggle's ("Switch to dark mode", "Switch to light mode") have no parameter. To set them for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <AppHeader>
            <AppBrand Label="Acme" Href="/" />
            <Box Grow />
            <ColorSchemeSwitch />
        </AppHeader>
        """;

    private const string Setup = """
        builder.Services.AddIzzyBlazor();
        """;
}
